# Goal 7: Export internal __redupi and __redupif

## Functions
`__redupi`, `__redupif`

## C Source
- /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/complexd/internal/ctrigd.c (or nearby)
- /home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/complexf/internal/ctrigf.c (or nearby)

## Rust Source
/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s2/src/complexd.rs and complexf.rs —
internal range reduction to [-pi, pi]

## Problem
The test harness calls `__redupi` and `__redupif` directly. These reduce an
argument modulo pi. They are not exported from the Rust binary.

Expected test outputs:
```
__redupi 0x1.921fb54442d18p+1 = -0x1.1a62633145c07p-53
__redupi 0x1.921fb54442d18p+2 = -0x1.1a62633145c07p-52
__redupi 0x1p-1 = 0x1p-1
__redupif 0x1.921fb6p+1 = 0x1.777a5cp-24
__redupif 0x1.921fb6p+2 = 0x1.777a5cp-23
__redupif 0x1p-1 = 0x1p-1
```

## What Needs to Change
Add `#[no_mangle] pub extern "C"` wrapper functions in lib.rs:
- `__redupi(x: f64) -> f64`
- `__redupif(x: f32) -> f32`

## Success Criteria
- All 6 test cases above produce bitwise-exact output matching C
